{
  "id": "one-column-margin-label",
  "name": "margin_label_one_column",
  "description": "One column with the section labels out in the left margin rather than over a rule: a narrow label track beside a wide text column, no horizontal rules anywhere, set in Palatino with a light unbolded name. Tightly set - the margin track is only as wide as the longest label, so the text column keeps nearly the full page. Sections run summary, education, skills, experience.",
  "disabled": false,
  "htmlContent": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title>{{name}} - Resume</title>\n<style>\n@page{margin:0.5in 0.55in}\n*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}\nhtml,body{background:#ffffff}\nbody{font-family:'Palatino Linotype','Book Antiqua',Palatino,Georgia,serif;font-size:10.5pt;line-height:1.38;color:#1c1917}\n/* THE DEVICE: each section is two tracks, and the heading lives in the narrow\n   one out in the left margin. One grid row per section, heading cell first, so\n   the PDF's text stream still reads heading-then-content - the reading order a\n   parser gets is paint order, and paint order here is DOM order. */\n.section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:0.92in minmax(0,1fr);gap:0 10px;margin-bottom:9px}\n/* NO LETTER-SPACING ON THESE. Tracking a 8.5pt label inside a narrow box makes\n   Chrome place the glyphs one at a time, and the PDF's text stream then reads\n   \"E D U C AT I O N\" - which matches nothing a parser is looking for. Measured,\n   not guessed: the same label without tracking comes out as one word. The\n   separation here is size, weight and colour instead. */\n/* The track is as wide as the LONGEST label and no wider - 0.92in holds\n   CERTIFICATIONS at this size, and every other label is shorter.\n   Measured, not chosen: a narrower track does not make the label hang into the\n   margin, it makes Chrome clamp the overflow at the box's left edge and push\n   the word right, where it collided with the content by 3px. `nowrap` keeps the\n   one long word from splitting mid-word instead. */\n.section-title{font-size:7.5pt;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;\n  color:#57534e;text-align:right;line-height:2.1;padding-top:1px}\n.section-body{min-width:0}\n/* NO RULES ANYWHERE. The margin column is the structure; a rule as well would be\n   saying the same thing twice. */\n.header{display:grid;grid-template-columns:0.92in minmax(0,1fr);gap:0 10px;margin-bottom:12px}\n.name{font-size:21pt;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0.2px;line-height:1.12}\n.headline{font-size:11pt;font-style:italic;color:#44403c;margin-top:2px}\n.contact{font-size:9.5pt;color:#44403c;margin-top:4px;line-height:1.45}\n.summary-text{color:#292524}\n.skill-category{margin-bottom:2px}\n/* Pinned to this template's ink so the six render-time looks cannot tint the\n   groups; the difference between a heading and its skills is weight and case. */\n.skill-category-title,.skill-category-skills{color:#1c1917}\n.skill-category-title{font-weight:700;font-size:9pt;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.6px}\n.skill-category-skills{font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal}\n.job-title{font-weight:700;font-size:11pt}\n.job-meta{font-size:9.5pt;color:#57534e;margin-top:1px}\n.exp-item{margin-bottom:7px}\n.exp-item:last-child{margin-bottom:0}\nul.achievements{margin:3px 0 0 15px}\nul.achievements li{margin-bottom:2px}\n.edu-item,.cert-item{margin-bottom:4px}\n.edu-item:last-child,.cert-item:last-child{margin-bottom:0}\n.edu-degree{font-weight:700}\n.edu-meta{font-size:9.5pt;color:#57534e}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"header\">\n<div></div>\n<div>\n<div class=\"name\">{{name}}</div>\n<div class=\"headline\">{{title}}</div>\n<div class=\"contact\">{{contact.phone}} &#183; {{contact.email}}{{#if contact.linkedin}} &#183; {{contact.linkedin}}{{/if}}{{#if contact.github}} &#183; {{contact.github}}{{/if}}{{#if contact.portfolio}} &#183; {{contact.portfolio}}{{/if}} &#183; {{contact.location}}</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"section\">\n<div class=\"section-title\">Summary</div>\n<div class=\"section-body\"><div class=\"summary-text\">{{summary}}</div></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"section\" style=\"break-inside:avoid;page-break-inside:avoid\">\n<div class=\"section-title\">Education</div>\n<div class=\"section-body\">\n{{#each education}}\n<div class=\"edu-item\">\n<div class=\"edu-degree\">{{degree}}</div>\n<div class=\"edu-meta\">{{institution}}{{#if location}} &#183; {{location}}{{/if}} &#183; {{startDate}} - {{endDate}}{{#if gpa}} &#183; GPA: {{gpa}}{{/if}}</div>\n</div>\n{{/each}}\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"section\">\n<div class=\"section-title\">Skills</div>\n<div class=\"section-body\"><div class=\"skills-line\">{{#if skillCategories.[0].category}}{{#each skillCategories}}<div class=\"skill-category\"><div class=\"skill-category-title\">{{category}}</div><div class=\"skill-category-skills\">{{join skills \", \"}}</div></div>{{/each}}{{else}}{{#if hardSkills.length}}{{#each hardSkills}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}{{else}}{{#each skills}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}{{/if}}{{/if}}</div></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"section\">\n<div class=\"section-title\">Experience</div>\n<div class=\"section-body\">\n{{#each experience}}\n<div class=\"exp-item\"><div style=\"break-inside:avoid;page-break-inside:avoid\">\n<div class=\"job-title\">{{title}}</div>\n<div class=\"job-meta\">{{company}}{{#if location}} &#183; {{location}}{{/if}} &#183; {{startDate}} - {{endDate}}</div>\n</div><ul class=\"achievements\">{{#each achievements}}<li>{{this}}</li>{{/each}}</ul>\n</div>\n{{/each}}\n</div>\n</div>\n\n{{#if certifications.length}}\n<div class=\"section\">\n<div class=\"section-title\">Certifications</div>\n<div class=\"section-body\">\n{{#each certifications}}\n<div class=\"cert-item\"><span class=\"edu-degree\">{{name}}</span>{{#if issuer}} &#183; {{issuer}}{{/if}}{{#if date}} &#183; {{date}}{{/if}}</div>\n{{/each}}\n</div>\n</div>\n{{/if}}\n</body>\n</html>",
  "cssContent": "",
  "sections": [
    "summary",
    "education",
    "hardSkills",
    "experience",
    "certifications"
  ],
  "createdAt": "2026-10-12T04:08:53.120Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-10-12T04:26:14.439137Z"
}
